# Docker/Podman build context filter.
#
# The Containerfile only consumes two directories from the build context:
# the ctx stage copies `build/` and `custom/` (see `COPY build /build` and
# `COPY custom /custom`). Everything listed below is never copied into the
# image, so excluding it keeps the context small and reproducible.
#
# NEVER add a pattern that hides `build/`, `custom/`, `Containerfile`, or the
# files those directories are expected to contain: `build/*.sh` reads
# `/ctx/build/**` and `/ctx/custom/**` (Brewfiles, ujust files, Flatpak
# preinstall files and custom/system-files) while the image is built.

# Version control and repository metadata
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.editorconfig
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# Agent scratch and tooling caches
.agents
.superpowers
.code-review-graph
.vscode
.ruff_cache

# Documentation and repository meta files not read at build time
docs
README.md
README.pt-BR.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
AGENTS.md
LOCAL-TESTING.md
LICENSE
artifacthub-repo.yml
cosign.pub
.hadolint.yaml

# Tests and automation are not part of the image context
tests
ci
n8n

# Local build artifacts, scratch dirs and disk/ISO images
output
_build-*
*.log
*.vhdx
iso
